IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hcfa-fumigation`

-- Hydrogen Cyanide (Fumigation) Act 1947, ss 2 to 6 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_hydrogen-cyanide-fumigation-act-1947.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `fixtures`

`a ship hold fumigated with hydrogen cyanide` MEANS Fumigation WITH
    `the gas` IS `hydrogen cyanide`
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS FALSE
    `carried out in the open air` IS FALSE

`a shophouse fumigated with hydrogen cyanide` MEANS Fumigation WITH
    `the gas` IS `hydrogen cyanide`
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS FALSE
    `carried out in the open air` IS FALSE

`timber stacked in a yard fumigated with hydrogen cyanide in the open air` MEANS Fumigation WITH
    `the gas` IS `hydrogen cyanide`
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS FALSE
    `carried out in the open air` IS TRUE

`a container fumigated with methyl bromide under a section 6 order` MEANS Fumigation WITH
    `the gas` IS `another substance`
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS TRUE
    `carried out in the open air` IS FALSE

`a container fumigated with methyl bromide with no order` MEANS Fumigation WITH
    `the gas` IS `another substance`
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS FALSE
    `carried out in the open air` IS FALSE

`an open-air fumigation with another gas under a section 6 order` MEANS Fumigation WITH
    `the gas` IS `another substance`
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS TRUE
    `carried out in the open air` IS TRUE

